{
  "id": null,
  "uid": "skp-flow",
  "title": "SKP Flow",
  "description": "Cross-service conservation for the SKP pipeline. The board to open first: it answers whether the system is broken and where, then links out to the source boards. The hop-gap panels span two services and belong to neither source board.",
  "tags": [
    "skp",
    "skp-flow",
    "pipeline"
  ],
  "timezone": "browser",
  "editable": true,
  "graphTooltip": 1,
  "schemaVersion": 39,
  "version": 0,
  "refresh": "30s",
  "time": {
    "from": "now-1h",
    "to": "now"
  },
  "timepicker": {},
  "links": [
    {
      "title": "SKP boards",
      "type": "dashboards",
      "tags": [
        "skp"
      ],
      "asDropdown": false,
      "includeVars": true,
      "keepTime": true,
      "targetBlank": false,
      "icon": "external link",
      "tooltip": "",
      "url": ""
    }
  ],
  "templating": {
    "list": [
      {
        "name": "datasource",
        "label": "Data source",
        "type": "datasource",
        "query": "prometheus",
        "refresh": 1,
        "hide": 0,
        "current": {},
        "options": []
      },
      {
        "name": "processor",
        "label": "Processor",
        "type": "query",
        "datasource": {
          "type": "prometheus",
          "uid": "${datasource}"
        },
        "definition": "label_values(pipeline_messages_produced_total{type=\"process-dispatch\"}, destination)",
        "query": {
          "qryType": 1,
          "query": "label_values(pipeline_messages_produced_total{type=\"process-dispatch\"}, destination)",
          "refId": "var-processor"
        },
        "refresh": 2,
        "sort": 1,
        "multi": true,
        "includeAll": true,
        "allValue": ".*",
        "hide": 0,
        "current": {
          "selected": true,
          "text": [
            "All"
          ],
          "value": [
            "$__all"
          ]
        },
        "options": []
      }
    ]
  },
  "annotations": {
    "list": []
  },
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "1 - Verdict: is the system broken?",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "System flowing",
      "description": "Total egress across every worker. Zero during a run means the pipeline has stopped, whatever else reads green.\n\n**Slow on purpose and slow by force.** $__rate_interval is 240s on this stack -- the datasource declares a 60s timeInterval because that is the OTLP export cadence, and Grafana floors the rate window at four times it. So this number averages the last four minutes and cannot fall to zero inside a shorter outage. Measured: with the whole pipeline stopped it still read 1.12 req/s a hundred seconds later, and through a sixty-second broker outage it only dipped 1.12 -> 0.92, never leaving green. Read the posture stats beside it for anything shorter than a few minutes; this one answers 'has throughput changed', not 'is it down'.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 3,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 1
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "expr": "sum(rate(pipeline_messages_produced_total[$__rate_interval])) or vector(0)",
          "legendFormat": "",
          "range": true,
          "editorMode": "code"
        }
      ],
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "orientation": "auto",
        "textMode": "auto",
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "area",
        "justifyMode": "auto"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "reqps",
          "decimals": 2,
          "mappings": [],
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": 0.0001
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Outbound hop gap",
      "description": "Dispatches the orchestrator confirmed, minus acks the processors issued, counted in MESSAGES over the visible range.\n\nCounts rather than a difference of rates, and the distinction is what makes the panel usable. Two counters scraped independently give a rate difference that is noise centred on zero -- measured here over an hour: p50 +0.000, max +0.074 req/s, tripping any near-zero threshold 13% of the time on a perfectly healthy stack. The same hour in counts: 1311 produced, 1313 acked. A real leak grows with the range; jitter does not.\n\n**A restart inside the range puts tens of messages here and none of them are lost.** A replica that goes away and comes back gets a new series, and produced and consumed counters for the same messages live on different services that restart at different moments. Measured across the chaos suite: +46/-47, +48/-46, +43/-44, every one an artefact of a scale-to-zero and every one gone within a range width. Check the Workers reporting stat before believing a number here.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 3,
        "x": 3,
        "y": 1
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "expr": "sum(increase(pipeline_messages_produced_total{type=\"process-dispatch\",outcome=\"accepted\"}[$__range])) - sum(increase(pipeline_messages_consumed_total{type=\"process-dispatch\",disposition=\"acked\"}[$__range])) or vector(0)",
          "legendFormat": "",
          "range": true,
          "editorMode": "code"
        }
      ],
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "orientation": "auto",
        "textMode": "auto",
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "area",
        "justifyMode": "auto"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "decimals": 0,
          "mappings": [],
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "orange",
                "value": -50
              },
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": -25
              },
              {
                "color": "orange",
                "value": 25
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 50
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Return hop gap",
      "description": "The same conservation check on the way back, in messages over the visible range.\n\nThe API also consumes step-outcome and that consumption is not instrumented, so a positive value here is the API's share before it is anything else.\n\nThresholded symmetrically with its outbound twin. The two measure one quantity in opposite directions, so a restart that puts +46 on one puts -47 on the other; with steps on the positive side only, the pair used to render one orange and one green for the same instant.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 3,
        "x": 6,
        "y": 1
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "expr": "sum(increase(pipeline_messages_produced_total{type=\"step-outcome\",outcome=\"accepted\"}[$__range])) - sum(increase(pipeline_messages_consumed_total{type=\"step-outcome\",disposition=\"acked\"}[$__range])) or vector(0)",
          "legendFormat": "",
          "range": true,
          "editorMode": "code"
        }
      ],
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "orientation": "auto",
        "textMode": "auto",
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "area",
        "justifyMode": "auto"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "decimals": 0,
          "mappings": [],
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "orange",
                "value": -50
              },
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": -25
              },
              {
                "color": "orange",
                "value": 25
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 50
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Retry amplification",
      "description": "Share of deliveries that will be redone, in MESSAGES over the visible range. Healthy is exactly zero.\n\nCounted rather than rated, and that is what makes it able to fire at all. As a ratio of two 240s rates it read 0.0% through every scenario in the chaos suite, including the broker outage that parked a delivery: one parked message against a 240s denominator is a rounding error, while one parked message in a fifteen-minute range is a number.\n\nGreen below 1%. Counting rather than rating makes this stat sticky for a range width, and thresholded red-at-any-non-zero it stayed red through the two scenarios AFTER the one that parked a single delivery -- 0.2% of traffic, on the board an operator opens first. A few redone messages is something to notice; a twentieth of all deliveries being redone is the outage.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 3,
        "x": 9,
        "y": 1
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "expr": "((((sum(increase(pipeline_messages_consumed_total{disposition=~\"requeued|parked\"}[$__range])) or vector(0)) > (sum(max_over_time(pipeline_messages_consumed_total{disposition=~\"requeued|parked\"}[$__range])) or vector(0))) or (sum(max_over_time(pipeline_messages_consumed_total{disposition=~\"requeued|parked\"}[$__range])) or vector(0))) + (((sum(increase(pipeline_messages_consumed_total{landed=\"false\"}[$__range])) or vector(0)) > (sum(max_over_time(pipeline_messages_consumed_total{landed=\"false\"}[$__range])) or vector(0))) or (sum(max_over_time(pipeline_messages_consumed_total{landed=\"false\"}[$__range])) or vector(0)))) / (sum(increase(pipeline_messages_consumed_total[$__range])) > 0) or vector(0)",
          "legendFormat": "",
          "range": true,
          "editorMode": "code"
        }
      ],
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "orientation": "auto",
        "textMode": "auto",
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "area",
        "justifyMode": "auto"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percentunit",
          "decimals": 1,
          "mappings": [],
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "orange",
                "value": 0.01
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 0.05
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      }
    },
